---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About AlbionForge"
  description="About AlbionForge: free fan-made profit calculators for Albion Online - refining, crafting, transport and enchanting, with verified math and no tracking."
  canonical="/about/"
>
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › About</div>
  <section class="section prose">
    <h1>About AlbionForge</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A guild accountant's toolkit for Albion Online - free, fan-made, and honest about its math.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge is a set of four profit calculators for Albion Online: <a
        href="/tools/refining/">refining</a>, <a href="/tools/crafting/">crafting</a>, <a
        href="/tools/transport/">city-to-city transport</a> and <a href="/tools/enchanting/"
        >artifact enchanting</a
      >. They answer one question quickly: <em>is this activity actually profitable at my prices?</em>
    </p>

    <h2>User-entered prices - a feature, not a limitation</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge deliberately does <strong>not</strong> pull live market data. There is no API key,
      no scrape, no delayed feed. You look at the in-game market (or your favorite market site) and
      type in the numbers you can actually trade at. Three reasons:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Accuracy.</strong> Stale “average price” feeds routinely lie about what you can really buy or sell at. Your own numbers never do.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy &amp; uptime.</strong> No data pipeline means no outages, no rate limits, and nothing to track you with.</li>
      <li><strong>Speed.</strong> Static pages that load instantly, anywhere - including on a second monitor mid-session.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where the game rules come from</h2>
    <p>
      Return rates, market tax structure, focus costs, refining recipes and city bonuses are baked
      into the calculators as editable presets, sourced from the
      <a href="https://albiononline.wiki.gg/" rel="noopener">Albion Online community wiki</a> and
      linked on each page. Every preset can be overridden, because patches change numbers and your
      in-game station fee is yours.
    </p>

    <h2>Who keeps the ledger</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge is built and maintained by a small team of Albion Online players who got tired of
      re-doing the same spreadsheets every patch. Pages and code are drafted with AI assistance and
      reviewed by the maintainer - every game number is checked against the sources listed on the
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>, where the testing setup is documented too.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact:</strong> forge@albionforge.top - corrections, bug reports and preset updates
      after game patches are welcome, and corrections are credited in the
      <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge is an unofficial, fan-made tool. Albion Online and all related properties are
      trademarks of Sandbox Interactive GmbH. This site is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or
      endorsed by Sandbox Interactive. No game assets are hosted here.
    </p>

    <Ornament />
    <p>
      Ready to run the numbers? Start with the <a href="/tools/refining/">refining calculator</a> or
      the <a href="/tools/transport/">transport arbitrage calculator</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
